["```php
class PasswordUpdateService {
    private $dao;
    private $authService;
    private $rateLimiter;
    private $messageCatalog;

    public function __construct(DAO $dao, AuthenticationService $authService, RateLimiter $rateLimiter, MessageCatalog $messageCatalog) {
        $this->dao = $dao;
        $this->authService = $authService;
        $this->rateLimiter = $rateLimiter;
        $this->messageCatalog = $messageCatalog;
    }

    public function updatePassword($userId, $password) {
        if (!$this->rateLimiter->allowRequest()) {
            throw new TooManyRequestsException($this->messageCatalog->get('too_many_requests'));
        }

        $isValid = $this->authService->validatePasswordPolicy($password);
        if (!$isValid) {
            throw new InvalidArgumentException($this->messageCatalog->get('invalid_password'));
        }

        try {
            $strength = $this->authService->evaluatePasswordStrength($password);
            if ($strength < 3) {
                throw new InvalidArgumentException($this->messageCatalog->get('weak_password', ['minimum' => 3]));
            }
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            // If the authentication service is down or experiencing issues, continue with the update.
            error_log($e->getMessage());
        }

        $this->rateLimiter->reset();
        $this->dao->beginTransaction();

        try {
            $user = $this->dao->findUserById($userId);
            if ($user === null) {
                throw new NotFoundException($this->messageCatalog->get('user_not_found'));
            }

            // Update the user's password in the database.
            $this->dao->updateUserPassword($userId, $password);
            $this->dao->commit();
        } catch (Exception $e) {
            $this->dao->rollback();
            throw $e;
        }
    }
}
```

This code snippet demonstrates a basic structure for the `PasswordUpdateService`. It uses Dependency Injection to create an instance of the service, including a DAO class for database operations, an AuthenticationService for password policy enforcement, a RateLimiter for request throttling, and a MessageCatalog for multi-language support.

The function `updatePassword()` first checks if the rate limit has been exceeded using the `RateLimiter`. If it has, it throws an exception. It then validates the password policy using the `AuthenticationService` and validates the password strength. If the validation fails, it throws an exception with an appropriate error message.

If the password is strong enough, it starts a database transaction, retrieves the user by their ID, and updates their password in the database. If any errors occur during this process, the transaction will be rolled back, ensuring data consistency."]

