["```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdbool.h>
#include <stddef.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <tbb/concurrent_vector.h>
#include <tbb/tbb_malloc.h>
#include <sys/syscall.h>
#include <time.h>

typedef struct {
    pthread_t thread_id;
    unsigned long long ue_id;
    tbb::concurrent_vector<void*> pdu_list;
} SMContext;

// Function to initialize and manage a list of session management contexts.
SMContext* create_sm_context(unsigned long long ue_id) {
    SMContext *context = (SMContext*)tbb::task::allocate_root();
    context->ue_id = ue_id;
    context->thread_id = syscall(SYS_gettid);
    return context;
}

// Function to add a PDU to an SMContext.
void add_pdu_to_sm_context(SMContext *context, void *pdu) {
    context->pdu_list.push_back(tbb::task::allocate_child());
    tbb::task::set_ref_count((char*)context->pdu_list.back(), 1);
    tbb::task::set_ref_count((char*)pdu, context->pdu_list.size());
    tbb::task::set_data_ref_count((char*)context->pdu_list.back(), 1);
    tbb::task::set_data_ref_count(pdu, context->pdu_list.size());
    context->pdu_list.back() = pdu;
}

// Function to remove a PDU from an SMContext by its index.
void remove_pdu_from_sm_context(SMContext *context, size_t index) {
    if (index >= context->pdu_list.size()) return;

    void* pdu = context->pdu_list[index];
    tbb::task::set_ref_count((char*)pdu, -1);
    context->pdu_list.erase(context->pdu_list.begin() + index);
}
```

This code creates an `SMContext` structure that includes a thread ID, UE identifier, and a concurrent vector (using Intel TBB's concurrent_vector) to manage the list of PDUs. The create_sm_context function initializes an SMContext with a unique UE identifier. The add_pdu_to_sm_context function adds a PDU to an SMContext by increasing the reference count for the PDU and the SMContext. The remove_pdu_from_sm_context function removes a PDU from an SMContext by decreasing its reference count and erasing it from the concurrent vector.

The code utilizes pthread for thread management, tbb::task::allocate_root() and tbb::task::allocate_child() to dynamically allocate memory for child tasks, and syscall(SYS_gettid) to obtain the current thread ID. The use of a concurrent vector ensures efficient addition and removal of PDUs under varying traffic loads while maintaining data integrity and performance in high-concurrency environments. Additionally, the code is modular, as it allows for future integration with external data sources for UE status updates and PDU metadata retrieval."]

